<section class="content">

<h2>Catechist Guide</h2>
<p class="big-question">For preparing and leading the class. For catechist use only.</p>

<h3>Class Summary</h3>

<p><strong>Estimated duration:</strong> 50-60 minutes (with activities, 90 minutes)</p>
<p><strong>Central theme:</strong> God reveals himself to human beings throughout history, culminating in Jesus Christ, the definitive Word. This revelation is transmitted by Tradition, Scripture, and the Magisterium.</p>
<p><strong>Objectives:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>That the student understand that revelation is God's initiative, not human discovery.</li>
<li>That they know the main stages of God's revelation in the Old Testament.</li>
<li>That they discover Jesus Christ as the full and definitive revelation of God.</li>
<li>That they understand how revelation is transmitted to us: Tradition, Scripture, Magisterium.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Key verse:</strong> Hebrews 1:1-2 (&laquo;Long ago at many times... he has spoken to us by a Son&raquo;)</p>
<p><strong>Catechism references:</strong> CCC 50-73, 74-100</p>

</section>

